course: dictionary
lesson: 12121
title: Combative and fighting words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Combative means ready and eager to fight or argue. Its clue is in the word itself: it sounds like combat, which means fighting. When you meet it, ask: is this person looking for a fight or an argument?
explain: In a story, «Mr Hart was so combative that he argued with everyone at the bus stop.» He is not just disagreeing once. The word tells you he likes to argue, and he goes looking for it.
explain: In sport, combative means playing hard and strongly against the other side. «The combative midfielder won every tackle» is praise: she is brave and determined. Read the rest of the sentence to see whether the word is good or bad.
explain: To check your meaning, put «ready to argue» into the sentence in place of combative. If it still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Combative means ready and eager to fight or argue.
fact: In sport, combative means playing hard and strongly against the other side.
fact: Combative sounds like combat, which means fighting.
fact: You can say a combative mood, a combative style or a combative player.
fact: Combative is an adjective: combative, more combative, most combative.
exercise: «The combative knight wanted to fight every visitor to the castle.» What does combative mean? | Lost and confused | *Ready and eager to fight | Very sleepy and calm
exercise: In a football report: «The combative defender tackled hard all match.» What does combative suggest here? | Watching quietly from the stands | *Playing hard against the other side | Playing badly and crying
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to combative? | *Argumentative | Peaceful | Gentle | Cheerful
test: «After the game, Ruby was in a combative mood and shouted at the referee.» What is a combative mood? | Feeling tired and hungry | Feeling calm and happy | *Feeling ready to argue or fight
test: Which phrase uses combative to describe sport? | *A combative player who never gives up | Gentle breeze | Sleepy cat | A combative picnic
exam: «The combative boy argued with every answer his teacher gave.» Which word means the same as combative? | Sleepy | *Quarrelsome | Generous | Shy
